{
  "_comment": "Instant replies for everyday talk -- no language model involved. Read by computer/voice/quick.py. 'match' phrases are compared to what you said after lower-casing, removing punctuation and filler words (hey, jarvis, please, ok, so, just, buddy...), so 'Goodnight, Jarvis!' matches 'goodnight'. 'say' = replies (one picked at random; {name} = your name); they're pre-recorded in JARVIS's voice. 'end' = end the conversation afterwards (back to waiting for 'hey Jarvis'). 'handler' = a built-in live reply or action instead of/in addition to 'say': time, date, day, weather, repeat, volume_up, volume_down, mute, unmute, briefing_ready. Edit freely -- restart voice wake (PA > Voice wake > Restart) to apply. 'defer_after_question' = if JARVIS just asked you a real question, a bare 'yes'/'good' goes to the model as your answer instead. 'offer' = after this reply, a 'yes' runs that (only 'briefing' for now). Conversation enders ('end': true -- JARVIS says its line and goes back to standby): besides exact matches, a short utterance (up to 8 words) that contains one of their phrases also ends it, unless it asks for something too (see quick.py _closer).",
